e traces: by the object's address (no reference: the object stays collectable), their totals and the"] [39 1 "// interned tracebacks; mu also orders the cleanups, which run on the collector's goroutine"] [47 18 "// a trace being made (its own allocations are none)"] [48 2 "// the C API's traces (PyTraceMalloc_Track, queue 594): a memory block of a domain, by (domain, address), in order"] [53 1 "// tmCKey is a C API trace's key: its domain and the block's address."] [66 18 "// (filename, lineno), most recent first"] [68 16 "// the interned frames' tuple, made at the first _get_traces"] [71 1 "// tracemallocStart is _PyTraceMalloc_Start."] [88 1 "// tmClear is _PyTraceMalloc_ClearTraces: the traces and the totals dropped (a pending cleanup of an old trace finds no"] [89 1 "// trace of its generation)."] [99 1 "// tmSize is a traced object's size: sys.getsizeof's (cpythonSizeof), a dict's 64, a cell's 40."] [110 1 "// tmAlloc records o's creation: its size and the running thread's traceback. A finalizer frees the trace. One argument:"] [111 1 "// the constructors' call stays cheap enough for Go's inliner (NewBytes, NewList, NewDict inlined as before)."] [168 1 "// tmTracebackOf is the running thread's traceback as tmAlloc makes it (the first nframe frames, interned); tm.mu held."] [199 1 "// ExtTraceMallocTrack is PyTraceMalloc_Track (Python/tracemalloc.c; arbace/pyctypes, queue 594): the block of size bytes at"] [200 1 "// ptr of the domain traced with the running thread's traceback (a trace of the same key replaced); -2 when tracemalloc is"] [201 1 "// not tracing."] [228 1 "// ExtTraceMallocUntrack is PyTraceMalloc_Untrack: the block's trace dropped (none: nothing); -2 when not tracing."] [243 1 "// tmCTraceback is _PyTraceMalloc_GetTraceback(domain, ptr): the block's traceback frames, None when it has no trace."] [257 1 "// tmFree is a traced object's collection: its trace dropped, when it is still the one of that generation."] [267 1 "// tmCleanup has tmFree run at o's collection: a finalizer (runtime.SetFinalizer: goi runs Go's own, where"] [268 1 "// runtime.AddCleanup's generic body is not interpretable); one per type, so a type another file finalizes is not"] [269 1 "// traced (an instance: 218's finalizer queue owns instances' finalization). A second finalizer on an object would be"] [270 1 "// Go's fatal error: o is always fresh here."] [285 1 "// tmCollect runs the collector and waits for the finalizers it queued (a sentinel's, queued last, run after theirs on"] [286 1 "// the one finalizer goroutine), so a dropped object's trace is gone; with the GIL released, at most a second a round."] [303 1 "// tmTracesList is _PyTraceMalloc_GetTraces: (domain, size, frames, total_nframe) per trace, frames interned."] [306 17 "// the list and tuples made here are no allocations of the program's (and tm.mu is held)"] [322 28 "// a key untracked and tracked again is in the order twice"] [384 4 "// the tables' sizes as Go holds them: a trace's entry and a traceback's frames"] [459 1 "// tracemallocAtStart is the configuration's tracemalloc (config_init_tracemalloc): PYTHONTRACEMALLOC=N (0 none) or"] [460 1 "// -X tracemalloc[=N] (the option wins) start it with N frames; a value that is no number is the configuration's error."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[128 18] [128 28] [148 32] [153 26] [173 19] [173 29] [192 32] [215 25] [236 25] [260 25] [289 17] [289 28] [445 34] [448 32] [463 44] [466 38] [471 46]]} (go/file "builtins_tracemalloc.go" :imports [


